    "result_text": "The full test suite (the acceptance tests are the only tests in the project) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, emitted alongside the existing human-readable audit line on successful owner creation.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Monotonic sequence** \u2014 added a static `AtomicLong OWNER_EVENT_SEQ`, shared across instances/requests and incremented once per successful create, giving the event stream a strict total order.\n\n2. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)`** \u2014 called right after the existing `AUDIT.info(...)` line; builds and logs the event.\n\n3. **Immutable event record `OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 a `record` (fields can't change after construction) serialized to compact JSON `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, with proper string escaping.\n\n4. **`primaryIdentifier(owner)`** \u2014 the single decision point for \"which field is the owner's primary identifier.\" It returns `customerCode` today; when a later checkpoint unifies the customer code into the member id, only this one method changes and the event will automatically carry the member id \u2014 satisfying the forward-looking requirement in the spec.\n\nThe emitted event looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` check (event line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the response's `customerCode`) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
